{"title":"02/11/2026","markdown":{"headingText":"02/11/2026","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"Had presentation, think it went decently.\n### Quick after presentation scratch notes:\n\nPresentation felt decent,\nWent a bit quicker speech wise than i wanted to\nThroat scratchy didnt help\nWas under time\nQuestions:\n- multiple recurrence, yes, inc side note on small system reccurence\n- how quantum error correction, gave practiced answer\n- logical qubit size, gave default answer for simple answer, wasnt real logical qbit answer, but i made clear i was talking about minimum example\n- real examples of this model, i gave impurity in condesned matter crystal, he one upped w/water molecules\n\nLast 3 were prof, hes a quantum computational guy\n\nProf was guy who wants to show hes smarter than you, i think i held my own, the power of \"this is beyond the scope but...\"\n\nI think my minor jokes (i.e big ugly correlation matrix) helped, i saw minor smiles at that\n\nLooking at audience, did better than most i think, but still looked at slides a bit too much\n\nDidnt pause for breath enough i think so went a bit fast\n\n\n\n## 04/11/2026\n\n### supervisor meeting\nQuickly recapped presentation - went fine, didn't need to cover that too much. Reiterated next steps of implementing metrics, then can examine memory effects. Discussed potential things that can be examined w/memory effects, discussion was a touch rambly/wide ranging but provided useful intuition inc:\n\n* adding narrow peak to spectral function - structure adds memory effects\n* relationship between fourrier transform of spectral function and memory effects (system/bath correlations? $\\mathcal{F}(J(\\omega))\\cdot f \\approx $ correlations)\n* need to seperate effects of structure and overall coupling - need to normalize coupling strength of spectral function \n* discussed some of David's work w/mpemba effect - discussed reentrance time and the gap between initially thermalized state and maximum deviation from that - this may be a useful \"mini-memory metric\"\n* Note - to extract thermalization numerically, can diagonalize $\\Lambda \\rho_{therm} = \\rho_{therm}$, when $\\rho_{therm}$ stabalises, is thermalized \n* can map out maximum deviation metric over $\\mu$ for $\\beta=10$ (see [@DavidMpemba2026] fig 2) - fig 2 phase diagram may be interesting to map out metrics over in general? tbd\n\nimmediate plan:\n\n* implement numeric thermalization determination from map\n* implement deviation gap mini metric\n* implement memory kernel def\n* examine metrics over $\\mu$ as outlined above\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["../../../styles.css"],